Marduk was with [[Kiel]] when he burned down the house of [[Sophie]] and [[Lucas Casterwill]], killing their parents. {{source|The Spiral War}}

Marduk rescued Kiel when he called for his [[Casterwill Hunters]] in [[Medusa's Cave]] and attempted to stop the [[Huntik Foundation]] team from retrieving Medusa's [[Amulet]]. {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}}

Upon the [[Blood Spiral]] ascertaining the location of [[Focauld Casterwill]], Marduk and Kiel went after Focauld's knowledge of the [[Casterwill family]]. The Huntik team, however, intervened and saved Focauld's [[Knowledgelock]] crystal from falling into the hands of the Spiral. {{Source|The Casterwill Connection}}

Marduk later tried to stop [[Den Fears]] and [[Lok Lambert]] from activating the [[Blue Star]] while Kiel attempted to take on [[Dante Vale]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]]. Their attempts, however, failed. {{Source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

[[Tantras]] asked him about the location of the Casterwills. {{Source|Sophie on Trial}} Shortly thereafter, Marduk fought alongside the Blood Spiral in the assault on the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. He gave chase to [[Santiago]] and fought with him, but later retreated when given the order by Tantras. {{Source|The Spiral War}}

Marduk took the place of [[Kiel]] in the [[Blooded Circle]], and spoke with [[Shauna]], [[Wind]], and [[Rassimov]] after the Huntik team retrieved Rassimov's secret files from his tenure within [[the Organization]]. {{Source|An Ally from the Organization}}

With the longest night of the year nearly at hand, Marduk was commanded by Rassimov to stop the Huntik team, after receiving orders from [[the Betrayer]] himself. He tracked the Huntik team down to [[Nostradamus' Tomb]] and ambushed them, invoking his [[Psikofen]] and [[Helinx]] Titans. He then fought against Dante and Lok, but Lok was able to use the [[Willblade]] to defeat him. The Huntik team then teleported to the [[Spiral Mark]] using [[Umbra]], leaving a seething Marduk behind. {{Source|Words from Eathon}}

